  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Kingdom National Commission for the United Nations Educational Scientific and Cultural Organisation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNESCO Constitution requires that Member States have a &#x2018;National Cooperating Body&#x2019; the purpose of which is designed to link government with the intellectual and scientific community in that country which works in UNESCO&#x2019;s fields of competence. The UK National Commission for UNESCO (UKNC) perform this function for the UK. The National Commission exists as a not for profit, created and funded for the purpose of being the UK&#x2019;s dedicated National Commission for UNESCO. UKNC work to coordinate the best independent expert advice and representation to enable FCDO and wider HMG to maximise the potential value for money of UNESCO&#x2019;s work.  The UK National Commission is funded through an Accountable Grant which provides for a small secretariat, supporting the provision of pro bono advice/expertise to government from a network of scientists, intellectuals and leaders in the fields of UNESCO competence.</narrative>
  </description>
